message: "If you use RISHI-Q, please cite this work."
title: "RISHI-Q: Beyond Metaphor — A Blinded Computational Test of Quantum-Structural Analogues in Classical Sanskrit Thought"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-16"
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shah
    given-names: Arjun
    email: arjunkshah21@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/arjunkshah12345-hash/rishi-q"
abstract: >
  RISHI-Q is a preregisterable computational framework for testing whether
  selected classical Sanskrit philosophical texts exhibit quantum-specific
  structural correspondences relative to matched historical controls, after
  source blinding, translation controls, vocabulary masking, and statistical
  safeguards. A negative result is a successful scientific result.
keywords:
  - computational humanities
  - philosophy of physics
  - Sanskrit philosophy
  - quantum foundations
  - reproducibility
